// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the build's pace
// THE BUILD'S PACE (r7; the method of the Hanging Gardens' builder). The engine hands the page back at the first ask
// that comes six milliseconds or more after the last hand-back, and every real hand-back waits for the next frame:
// a build that asks after every small piece is cut into pieces of six or seven milliseconds and spends a frame on
// each, so its whole time is the count of its pieces times a frame. This world's asks therefore go through a count
// of work: each ask says about how many milliseconds the piece that FOLLOWS it takes (read from the build's own
// trace on a quiet machine: the figures stand in the code beside each ask; BUILD_PACE.PLAIN where none is said),
// and the engine is asked only when what is gathered since the last asking and the piece to come are together more
// than BUILD_PACE.PIECE, or when the piece to come is a dear one (DEAR and more) and SOME work is gathered already.
// NO CLOCK IS READ. Nothing a visitor sees hangs on it: no stream is drawn more, fewer or in another order.
// (PIECE is kept small: on a busy machine every piece takes several times its quiet figure, and code run for the
// first time is slow; with 2.5 the build's pieces stay near the engine's own six milliseconds.)
export const BUILD_PACE = { PIECE: 2.5, DEAR: 2, SOME: 0.5, PLAIN: 1 };
const HANDED = Promise.resolve();
export function makePace(yieldNow = async () => {}) {
  let got = 0;
  return (next = BUILD_PACE.PLAIN) => {
    if (got > 0 && (got + next > BUILD_PACE.PIECE || (next >= BUILD_PACE.DEAR && got >= BUILD_PACE.SOME))) { got = next; return yieldNow(); }
    got += next; return HANDED;
  };
}

