//     the hour's own sun colour at the face's height, CASING_SHEEN strong. Never a spot, never a mirror: nothing is
//     reflected in it. It is light by the law of the stone, the same for any eye at that place; as the eye goes
//     round the pyramid the glow slides over the lit face. A face in shade has none. THE BEAM IS SHARED between the
//     two: CASING_MATT of it the stone gives back matt (to every side alike), the rest goes into the sheen; of the
//     sky's broad light and the ground's the stone gives back its whole white, as before (a broad light's sheen goes
